.S.-engineered battery management and analytics platform. Eos Energy Enterprises, Inc. was formerly known as B. Riley Principal Merger Corp. II and changed its name to Eos Energy Enterprises, Inc. in November 2020. The company was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph R. Mastrangelo Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $847,259 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 787 people. Revenue per employee of $145K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 249%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $32K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Eos Energy Enterprises, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $700M market cap on $114M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +85% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -700% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and -330% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $265M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -9.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-3.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (37.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 236% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2330957.89},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 58/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 139% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Eos Energy Enterprises (NASDAQ:EOSE) & NuScale Power (NYSE:SMR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-eos-energy-enterprises-nasdaqeose-nuscale-power-nysesmr.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584692.0,"origin":"